# Design Binding — claude-design

`DESIGN.md` `## Screens × form factors` lists component **names** only. The per-element detail
— text labels, badges, hint text, timestamp **format**, app-shell chrome, control order — lives in
the exported bundle under `docs/design/<id>/`. Implementing from the name list alone drops elements
silently. This skill closes that gap mechanically.

The agent has already read `DESIGN.md`. For every screen a UI task implements (plan time) or has
implemented (implement time), run the three steps below. The export bundle is **user-owned and
read-only** — never edit files under `docs/design/<id>/`.

## Step 1 — Locate the artifact

In `DESIGN.md § Screens × form factors`, each screen row links into the exported bundle under
`docs/design/<EPIC-SEQ>/screens/`. Exports are `<name>-<form-factor>.<ext>`:

- **HTML export** (`.html`) → `Read` it. Full element diff possible (Step 2).
- **Image-only export** (`.png` / `.jpg`, no HTML) → you cannot parse a raster. Fall back to
  `DESIGN.md`'s per-screen detail and `components.md` if the bundle ships one, and raise ONE flag
  per image-only screen (see Step 3, image-only case).

## Step 2 — Build the element manifest

From the HTML export's rendered content (or `components.md` when present), enumerate every
user-visible element, in order:

- text labels + their exact copy (headings, button labels, link text)
- badges / chips / status pills
- hint / helper / placeholder / error text (e.g. a field hint, a keyboard-shortcut line)
- timestamps **and their format** — relative ("2 hours ago") vs absolute ("May 29, 2026"). The
  format is part of the spec.
- icons + their accessible labels
- sub-components nested inside a row / card — including a child element a later feature added to a
  component an earlier feature defined (e.g. a badge added to an existing list row)
- app-shell chrome: header, page title, nav, toolbar buttons + their labels
- control order within a group (e.g. Save before Cancel)

Ignore any export-tool scaffolding (annotation layers, redline overlays) — only ship what the
screen itself renders.

## Step 3 — Diff against the code + flag

For each manifest element, confirm the implemented component renders it (or, at plan time, that a
task covers it). For any element present in the manifest but absent from the code **and** not in
the task scope / PLAN.md file plan, append to `docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/FLAGS.md` (create if
absent):

```
### AF-<next>: inconsistency · task: T-NN · <code-file>
design element "<element>" on screen <S> present in claude-design export but not implemented — DESIGN.md component list omitted it.
```

**Image-only screen** (no HTML to diff): raise instead

```
### AF-<next>: risky-pattern · task: T-NN · docs/design/<id>/screens/<S>
visual fidelity for screen <S> not auto-verified — export is image-only; DESIGN.md component list may under-specify elements. Confirm by eye at /arh-human-review.
```

`<next>` is the next sequential AF id. Triaged at `/arh-human-review` before commit-PR. Never silently
skip an element because the component "looks done."

## Contract (uniform across all design providers)

- **Input:** `DESIGN.md` (already read) + the provider artifact for each screen.
- **Output:** zero or more `AF-NN` flags; the UI verified element-complete against the artifact.
- **Read-only** on the design source. Never weaken: a missing element is always a flag.

